  "Question": "The inequality \\(x^2-2x+m>0\\) holds for every real number \\(x\\). The discriminant must be less than 0. What is the discriminant when \\(m=2\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "-4",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The discriminant is \\(4-8=-4\\), which is less than 0. The parabola opens upward, so the expression is indeed always positive in this case.",
